{"duration_api_ms":207602,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"18a73502-0915-4566-92d7-dca84caa467e","total_cost_usd":0.25369200000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16167,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13491},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16167,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18902,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16167},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18902,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16167,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25369200000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13491,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front has converged onto one corner: D~3.385, b=1.2, cone=70, with flight-path angle (gamma) as the only free variable. Three walls box it in. The mass-fraction margin is about 0 at D~3.3852 (cone 70 is the flattest, lightest forebody). The cd_fore surrogate hull refuses b>1.2 at cone 70. Peak g reaches 12 at gamma~-3.570. Along the front, steeper gamma raises flux (227k to 275k W/m2) and lowers bondline T (418 to 391 K). The last three rounds added only about 0.0002 hypervolume each.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-4d63379171a2 (gamma -3.57, g margin 5e-5, mass margin 2.6e-4) and C-1a745bbcb46d, C-092723c51b5a show the corner is boxed in by both the g and mass walls.\",\"C-507815483127, C-e6aafb4787d2, C-b31977b067c2, C-b59eb448d6ee and C-3d41ce848a30 show b>1.2 at cone 70 fails on the surrogate hull.\",\"C-c708a99f10f1, C-17a9b770e63c and C-a55828a3ab03 show cone<=67 at b>=1.2 is an invalid geometry (nose and shoulder overlap).\",\"C-71f892c85980 (D 3.2) and C-c050b796618a (D 3.3, b 1.17) are worse in T at the g wall, so smaller D is dominated. C-1d2c34a68964 (b 1.1) is slightly worse than b 1.2.\",\"Mass margin fits 1-k*D^2 at D=3.384/3.3845/3.3848/3.385, and reaches 0 near D=3.3852.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set mainly by gamma (about 1.67 g/deg), so gamma is capped near -3.570. Bondline T follows heat load, which falls with larger nose radius b*D and lower ballistic coefficient. Both are capped by the mass wall (D) and the hull wall (b). Flux falls roughly as D^-1.5, so the largest feasible D dominates. What is left is small: push D to the mass limit across the gamma sweep, and probe cone angles just under 70 and lower b to see whether the hull, geometry and mass walls leave any room. This relies on the data plus prior Sutton-Graves reasoning.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass margin near D=3.3852 is extrapolated linearly, so a few D-max proposals may fail on mass. Whether the hull admits cone<70 at b~1.2, and how much mass and area a lower cone adds, is untested. Effects of b and cone on T are only inferred from a few points. The predicted gain from the D-refinement points is very small.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-4d63379171a2\",\"rationale\":\"Raise D to the mass limit at the g-wall gamma. Larger D lowers flux by about 1.5x the relative D change and lowers T slightly.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274570,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mass-wall extrapolation (margin predicted ~8.6e-5) at the front's corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4d63379171a2\",\"rationale\":\"Push D almost to the predicted mass zero-margin, at slightly shallower gamma so g stays under 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5695},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274560,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the exact mass wall. Predicted margin is ~2.7e-5, so it may fail.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4d63379171a2\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly less steep gamma at D=3.3851 keeps g margin while using the larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274315,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.18,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a robustly feasible near-corner front point with the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2bcf209a7e05\",\"rationale\":\"Existing front point at gamma -3.45 used D=3.3845. Larger D should dominate it slightly.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271720,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.26,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominance improvement along the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-354edad0eb7a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front at gamma -3.3 with the largest feasible D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268160,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.78,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolated front point at the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9902cb6914c6\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at gamma -3.0 with D at the mass limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.02,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves mid-front coverage and dominance.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-13cb80918fed\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front at gamma -2.5 with larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominance gain over C-13cb80918fed.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5b73c6848389\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.87 and -2.17 at gamma -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237650,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.03,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage at the low-flux, high-T end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a2cf6bb4f3a8\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between gamma -1.65 and -1.87 with the larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-flux end coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a565d31e5d1c\",\"rationale\":\"Low-flux extreme of the front at the gamma bound, with larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227210,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.88,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Marginally better endpoint of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a slightly lower cone angle (69.5) at b=1.2, with D reduced to compensate for a possible mass increase.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"diameter_m\":3.36},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shows how cone angle trades area/mass against Cd, and whether the hull admits cone<70 at b=1.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69 at b=1.2 with smaller D. Tests where the geometry wall and hull begin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"diameter_m\":3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the cone-angle sensitivity of flux, T and mass at the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 68.7 at b=1.2 is near the geometry-overlap boundary implied by the cone-67 failure (about -42 mm at D 3.3). Locates that boundary.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.7,\"diameter_m\":3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether b=1.2 tolerates cone<70. If it fails, it bounds the feasible geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d2c34a68964\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.15 with cone 69 and D 3.36: an intermediate point between the b=1.1 and b=1.2 designs.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the b/cone trade-off inside the hull.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d2c34a68964\",\"rationale\":\"Lower b (1.05) with cone 68 and D 3.36 to see whether a lower-cone, lower-b region is competitive.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Explores whether a different (b, cone) pair reaches a lower-T region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.19 at D=3.3851 tests smoothness of the b-effect just inside the hull edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19,\"diameter_m\":3.3851},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the hull is not narrower than b=1.2 at D=3.3851 and gives a local b-gradient.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d2c34a68964\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.0 at cone 70 with D 3.37 (kept within the mass wall) to quantify the b-sensitivity of flux and T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates the b-effect for a lower-b trade region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69.8 with D 3.375 to check whether a very small cone reduction still lies in the hull and stays under the mass wall.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.8,\"diameter_m\":3.375},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fine sensitivity to cone angle near the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69.9 with D 3.383. A minimal cone step, to see whether the hull edge at b=1.2 is sharp in cone.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"diameter_m\":3.383},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a local cone gradient close to the optimum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d2c34a68964\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.17 with cone 69.5 and D 3.37 at gamma -3.55, a nearby variant that stays inside the geometry limits.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.17,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests a nearby (b, cone) combination for hull and mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d2c34a68964\",\"rationale\":\"Low-b, lower-cone variant (b 0.9, cone 66, D 3.35) to check whether a different area/drag trade beats the corner. Mass is expected to be marginal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Diversifies the sampling into a lower-b, lower-cone region to check whether any point there is non-dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":162536,"type":"result","duration_ms":207638,"uuid":"a708ca91-f783-45cb-8794-eda292838c0c","ttft_stream_ms":1585,"time_to_request_ms":34,"first_content_frame_ms":1585,"queued_turn_count":0,"resul